From: Wave7 development
Subject: net: ethernet: qualcomm: edma: wake the completed TX queue

TX descriptor and completion rings are mapped one-to-one in per-port
queue order. The CPU executing completion need not be the CPU selecting
the TX queue. Waking the latter by using the current CPU can strand
nonzero queues when all completion IRQs are on CPU0.

Use the completion ring's queue index, pair queue stop with a fresh
hardware consumer-index read, and start/stop all queues during port
lifecycle. Do not stop queues on DMA mapping errors, which need not
produce any completion.

